6 - File Guide
    ----------

    L003_00_Premises.v

      Stdlib imports and the primitive records: `DiagonalStructure`,
      `CertificationStructure`, `FaithfulInterpretation`, `SizeFreeLanguage`,
      `SizeFreeInterpretation`, `ProvabilityCalculus`, `LanguageCalculus`,
      and the law records `HilbertKS`, `DerivabilityConditions`,
      `LanguageBoxRepresentation`, `CertifiedNegDupRules`. Defines
      evaluation, acceptance, soundness, completeness, the diagonal sentence
      and claim, decidable semantics, bounded families, ascent levels, and
      predicativity.

    L003_01__Diagonal_Ascent.v

      Lawvere's fixed-point theorem, no point-surjection to `bool`, diagonal
      escape, Evaluator Ascent, the global and local absence of an internal
      total classifier, and emptiness of diagonal-closed levels under
      strictly increasing formation levels.

    L003_02__Certification_Dichotomy.v

      Projection of a sound and complete verifier evaluates its level;
      Certification Ascent; self-application and the certification fixed
      point; the dichotomy as decided acceptance, its exclusivity, and its
      decidable-semantics instance; and the sharpness structure with
      `dichotomy_sharpness`.

    L003_03__Invariance_Size_Free.v

      Faithful and size-free invariance, the size-free fixed point, pointwise
      incompleteness, the sharp constructive boundary, the internal truth
      obstruction, `forget_levels`, and `trivial_grading`.

    L003_04__Ascent_Hierarchy.v

      Diagonal beyond domain, impossibility of impredicative closure,
      predicativity of correct certifiers, the ascent hierarchy, its
      two-sided bound, and proliferation.

    L003_05__Internal_Certification.v

      Derived Hilbert rules, Löb, Gödel II, the language-level fixed point,
      language-level Gödel II, and `consistent_certifies_neither`.

    L003_06__Concrete_Language.v

      Terms with an oracle node, bit-stream pairing, relativized semantics
      and its extensionality, the prefix-free serialization with unique
      parsing, the serialization grading, and `concrete_structure O`.

    L003_07__Exhaustive_Evaluation.v

      Reindexing and its semantic lemma, quotation matching, enumeration of
      every level, `brute_force`, `concrete_certifier`, the concrete bounded
      family, the concrete hierarchy and proliferation, and relativization.

    L003_08__Plain_SAT.v

      Propositional formulas, truth tables and `classify_correct`, circuit
      verifiers with Boolean reflection, specialization, the Solver's
      Paradox for plain SAT, and the two minimal branches.

    L003_09__Tseitin_CNF.v

      Clauses and CNF, Tseitin conversion, its equisatisfiability and linear
      bounds, and clause-level specialization of circuit verifiers.

    L003_10__Coding_Sensitivity.v

      The concrete language under an arbitrary quotation, the fixed point
      under every quotation, injectivity of the standard and negated
      quotations, the branch flip of `TBit 0`, and the failure of recoding to
      be faithful.

    L003_11__Evaluator_Lower_Bound.v

      Read positions and their extensionality, the cost of reading, the
      one-bit pairs `TBit i` and `TBit (i + 1)`, the read obligation of every
      evaluator, and the quadratic lower bound `(n - 4) (n + 2)`.

    L003_12__Relativized_SAT.v

      Boolean oracles, oracle formulas with constant-or-variable arguments,
      relativized truth tables and their agreement with `classify` on
      oracle-free formulas, oracle circuits, relativized specialization, and
      the relativized Solver's Paradox.

    L003_95_API.v

      Stable public API: thirty-eight named contracts, `L003_CORE_CONTRACT`,
      and `L003_CONTRACT`.

    L003_97_Artifacts.v

      Certifies `l003_core_qed` and `l003_contract_qed`, redirects their
      assumption reports, and extracts the executable layer to OCaml.

    L003_98_Sanity.v

      Closed computations for grading, reindexing, enumeration, truth tables,
      circuit recognition, specialization, and Tseitin conversion, and
      endpoint inhabitation checks.

    INDEX

      Ground-truth index: one entry per contract with its endpoint, the
      file and line of every theorem it uses, a plain statement, its
      premises, and whether it is unconditional. The paper cites only from
      this index.

    _appendix/_artifacts/

      Extracted OCaml: `L003_Plain_SAT.{ml,mli}`, containing quotation and
      grading, `reindex`, `match_bits`, `terms_upto`, `brute_force`,
      `concrete_certifier`, `classify`, `circuit_verifierb`,
      `specialized_formula`, `tseitin`, and `cnf_eval`. The build guard
      checks that the checked-in files equal the freshly generated ones.

    _appendix/_assumptions/

      Redirected `Print Assumptions` output for `l003_core_qed` and
      `l003_contract_qed`. Both are closed.


