      CODING_SENSITIVITY_CONTRACT
      EVALUATOR_LOWER_BOUND_CONTRACT
      RELATIVIZED_SAT_CONTRACT

      L003_CORE_CONTRACT, L003_CONTRACT

    Certified endpoints:

      l003_core_qed     : L003_CORE_CONTRACT
      l003_contract_qed : L003_CONTRACT

    Principal theorems:

      coding_free_identity : forall C v x,
        ds_sem C (diagonal_sentence C v) x <->
        ~ exists w, ds_sem C v (ds_pair C (ds_pair C x x) (cs_wit C w))

      certification_fixed_point : forall C v,
        DiagonalClaim C v <-> ~ DiagonalAccepted C v

      certification_dichotomy : forall C v,
        (DiagonalAccepted C v \/ ~ DiagonalAccepted C v) <->
        CertificationFailsAtDiagonal C v

      dichotomy_sharpness :
        (forall C v, (DiagonalClaim C v -> DiagonalAccepted C v) ->
                     CertificationFailsAtDiagonal C v) <->
        (forall Q : Prop, Q \/ ~ Q)

      concrete_certification_family : forall O,
        BoundedCertificationFamily (concrete_structure O) concrete_certifier

      solvers_paradox_plain_sat : forall O v,
        CircuitVerifier v ->
        formula_size (specialized_formula v) <= term_size v /\
        (classify (specialized_formula v) = true <->
         Satisfiable (specialized_formula v)) /\
        (term_level (diagonal_term v) = term_level v + 9 /\
         (BF at the level of g_v settles the diagonal claim) /\
         forall B n, term_level (diagonal_term v) <= n ->
           Evaluates (concrete_structure O) B n ->
           term_level v + 3 < term_level B) /\
        (ConcreteDiagonalClaim O v <-> ~ Satisfiable (specialized_formula v)) /\
        (exactly one of the two branches)


8 - Notes
    -----

    L003 depends only on Stdlib. It does not import M001: its Hilbert calculus
    is abstract, carries a box operator, and states its laws as separate
    records.

    Concrete costs are exact: negation, duplication, and projection each add
    a three-bit tag, binary connectives add three bits plus both operands,
    and constants have level four.

    `BF_n` is a definability witness, not an algorithm. `terms_upto`
    over-approximates each level and grows doubly exponentially, so the
    extracted `brute_force` is total but usable only at levels below four.

    Every internal evaluator of level `n` has level at least
    `(n - 4) (n + 2)`, while the constructed `BF_n` has level at least
    `3^(n+1) - 3`. The quadratic bound depends on the unary index encoding;
    under binary indices the same argument is much weaker. Whether a
    polynomial-size evaluator exists is open.

    The internal premises are satisfiable: `INTERNAL_MODEL_CONTRACT` gives a
    consistent Gödel-Löb calculus over the natural numbers with a certified
    fixed point of `~ box`, and a consistent language calculus whose box is
    the atomic claim of the projected verifier and which satisfies every
    premise of the language-level fixed point and Gödel II. D1-D3 for a
    proof-checking calculus inside the concrete language, with box as
    projection of an actual verifier, are a separate project.

    Open obligations, not formalized: the gap between the quadratic and the
    exponential bound; and concrete D1-D3.

    Freeze: from the release tag on, no renames and no new contracts; only
    bug fixes, and any change to a statement is reported before it is made.
    The build is pinned to the Rocq version in `_tools/ROCQ_VERSION`.
